{
  "summary": "The experiment tested an RNA-only model using PCA-reduced features without image data or fusion, achieving validation accuracy of 0.4849 and F1 of 0.4639. This performance is lower than multimodal baselines (0.526–0.523 accuracy), suggesting RNA-only approaches may underperform compared to multimodal integration. Uncertainty remains about the necessity of multimodal strategies, as this baseline does not isolate modality interaction effects."
}

